Standard Array vs. ArrayList

                                                         ********** Declaration *********
• Primitive Variable: int num = 10;
• Standard Array (Empty with Size): int[] arr = new int[5];
• Standard Array (With Values): int[] arr = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
• ArrayList (Empty): ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
• ArrayList (With Values): ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(10, 20, 30));
• List Interface (Best Practice): List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();

Feature                 	Standard Array (int[])	                                  ArrayList (ArrayList<Integer>)
Size      	              Fixed once created	                                     Dynamic (grows automatically)
Data Type	                Holds primitives (int)	                                 Holds objects (Integer)
Adding Items	            arr[0] = 10;	                                           result.add(10);
Getting Items	            arr[0]	                                                 result.get(0)
Checking Length	          arr.length	                                             result.size()

